# Preserved review and reading evidence

The September 14–15 review records are unchanged copies recovered from
`.git/codex/`, not new reviews or endorsements. [`manifest.json`](manifest.json)
records each historical path, ordinary path, size, and SHA-256. The copies were
hash-checked before redundant hidden originals were retired; use the mapping
when an old historical link no longer points at ordinary project storage. The
separately listed September 7 authoring trial was recovered from its named local
branch and has its own provenance record.

- [Pro mathematical audit](pro-review-2026-09-15/thesis_review/03_mathematical_audit.md),
  [examiner report](pro-review-2026-09-15/thesis_review/01_examiner_report.md),
  and [complete package](pro-review-2026-09-15/thesis_review/README.md): the
  original returned package, including annotated PDF, findings, and verification
  scripts/results. The reviewer's supplied arguments remain reviewer-supplied.
- [Frozen pre-Pro self-review](calibration/self-review-2026-09-15-pre-pro.md)
  and [comparison with Pro](calibration/pro-comparison-2026-09-15.md).
- [Blind self-review](blind-self-review-2026-09-15/REPORT.md), with its freeze
  record and inspected text/images.
- [HKO reading feedback](calibration/hko-reading-feedback.md),
  [DS human reading feedback](human-feedback/ds-reading-2026-09-14.md), and
  [18:00 retrospective](calibration/1800-checkpoint-retrospective.md).
- [HKO authoring trial](calibration/hko-authoring-trial-2026-09-07/README.md):
  the three compared explanation candidates, exact human-reading input, later
  repaired preview, and their bounded provenance and approval limits.

The unannotated frozen thesis is preserved separately at
[`source-recovery/evidence/frozen.pdf`](../source-recovery/evidence/frozen.pdf).
The recovered candidate's identity and clean-build checks are in
[`source-recovery/README.md`](../source-recovery/README.md).

This is a bounded preservation of existing review records, not a complete
archive of chat transcripts, all historical drafts, or all project evidence.
The Pro scripts were copied, not rerun during source recovery. The coordinator
includes these preserved files in the scoped preparation checkpoint.
